\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"postgresql-server/contrib 16.14 installed and rpm-verified on all three nodes; node2's initial install failed on a transient GPG-key parse error and was successfully retried.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-fde095301b2d4072\",\"cmd-719d7afc95d54941\",\"cmd-830cf008db4247aa\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"node1 configured as writable streaming-replication primary\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"initdb run on node1, replicator role created, postgresql.conf set wal_level=replica/max_wal_senders/max_replication_slots/hot_standby, pg_hba.conf opened scram-sha-256 replication access for node2/node3, service restarted and confirmed active with the new settings applied.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e8114efc063f4d49\",\"cmd-eddea8bc77e14865\",\"cmd-2d6ad93e20304d36\",\"cmd-cb05b3bd65794833\",\"cmd-36dd3f6e5a0c4282\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 configured as read-only standbys streaming from node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Dedicated physical replication slots created on the primary; pg_basebackup -R cloned the primary onto both standbys (standby.signal + primary_conninfo present); both standbys started and pg_stat_replication on the primary shows both walreceivers in streaming/async state; INSERT attempts on both standbys were rejected with a read-only-transaction error.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-9e124f2f19324919\",\"cmd-535d97b1d44e4183\",\"cmd-3a3ba3f9e35b4cf5\",\"cmd-9b1e3329dd8c4739\",\"cmd-71ba2da44b0c4283\",\"cmd-8d09da3b160843d2\",\"cmd-a1074fdb0f0a4540\",\"cmd-ab895597e9524e50\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Changes committed on the primary are visible on both standbys\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A table was created and rows inserted on node1; both standbys immediately showed the identical rows via SELECT. This was re-verified after a full restart cycle, when a new row inserted on the restarted primary also replicated to both standbys.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-4bc34b04da1e4d7b\",\"cmd-a1074fdb0f0a4540\",\"cmd-ab895597e9524e50\",\"cmd-b993f414a9fe46bf\",\"cmd-97e051fbaf9a48f7\",\"cmd-204efbb313824935\"]}],\"confidence\":0.93,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"Executor commands map cleanly to task steps (install, initdb, role/config, slots, basebackup, verification). Two bounded self-corrected mutations occurred: an initial openssl-based password generation failed (openssl absent) and was immediately replaced with a working urandom-based generator (cmd-2135debd7ec34bc3 -> cmd-6568c33047f54f97); and pg_basebackup on node2/node3 was first invoked with a redundant -C flag that collided with the already-created slots and auto-wiped the target data directory before a corrected retry succeeded (cmd-833a9afd0d184228, cmd-b1e3e32dd06947c9 -> cmd-535d97b1d44e4183/cmd-3a3ba3f9e35b4cf5). Neither left residue: the plaintext replication-password files were explicitly removed on all three nodes (cmd-2629cf4a4c834a7d, cmd-9b1e3329dd8c4739, cmd-71ba2da44b0c4283) after use. Cluster-wide passwordless SSH and firewalld postgresql exposure were opened, which are reasonable, bounded prerequisites for password transfer and inter-node replication traffic rather than unnecessary changes. Post-executor snapshots show no failed services and no unexplained residue beyond expected install/reboot log files.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2135debd7ec34bc3\",\"cmd-6568c33047f54f97\",\"cmd-833a9afd0d184228\",\"cmd-b1e3e32dd06947c9\",\"cmd-535d97b1d44e4183\",\"cmd-3a3ba3f9e35b4cf5\",\"cmd-2629cf4a4c834a7d\",\"cmd-9b1e3329dd8c4739\",\"cmd-71ba2da44b0c4283\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node2:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node3:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task are directly satisfied: node1 was configured as a writable primary, node2 and node3 were built as read-only physical standbys via pg_basebackup with dedicated replication slots and confirmed streaming, standby writes were shown to be rejected, and primary writes were shown to propagate to both standbys both before and after a full one-at-a-time restart of all three nodes. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was executed thoroughly: pre-restart baselines, reboot acknowledgements, boot-identity changes, and post-restart recovery/replication/data checks were captured for node2, node3, and node1 (primary), and the observed boot IDs match the fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshot exactly, corroborating the trace.\",\"limitations\":[\"Evidence for standby read-only/streaming state and data visibility relies on psql output captured shortly after actions; no long-duration steady-state monitoring was captured, though this is not required by the task.\",\"The prepare phase was disabled (after_prepare is an alias of before_prepare), so all observed state changes are attributable to the executor.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"PostgreSQL server installed on node1, node2, and node3","status":"satisfied","summary":"postgresql-server/contrib 16.14 installed and rpm-verified on all three nodes; node2's initial install failed on a transient GPG-key parse error and was successfully retried.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fde095301b2d4072","cmd-719d7afc95d54941","cmd-830cf008db4247aa"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"node1 configured as writable streaming-replication primary","status":"satisfied","summary":"initdb run on node1, replicator role created, postgresql.conf set wal_level=replica/max_wal_senders/max_replication_slots/hot_standby, pg_hba.conf opened scram-sha-256 replication access for node2/node3, service restarted and confirmed active with the new settings applied.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e8114efc063f4d49","cmd-eddea8bc77e14865","cmd-2d6ad93e20304d36","cmd-cb05b3bd65794833","cmd-36dd3f6e5a0c4282"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"node2 and node3 configured as read-only standbys streaming from node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dedica